// "Calls back a soul that left its body only moments ago" -- a true
// death-reversal, but this engine has no addressable "dead" state to revive
// into: `Health::revive()` (common/src/comp/health.rs) exists only for
// admin/banishment/respawn code paths, not as a `CombatEffect` any spell RON
// can invoke, and adding one is Rust (Lane B), out of scope here. Same
// class of gap spare_the_dying.ron (this folder) already documents for the
// lighter "stabilize a dying creature" case -- "no dedicated downed/dying
// state exists... modeled as a modest instant heal on the touched ally, the
// closest existing primitive". This spell scales that exact same
// simplification up: `SelfBuff` cannot reach a touched ally (see
// spare_the_dying.ron's own header), so `BasicMelee` +
// `attack_effect_target: InGroup` delivers the largest heal in this cell,
// reflecting "returns a creature to life" as the strongest revival-adjacent
// effect this engine can express, one step past life_transference.ron's own
// touch-ally heal in this same folder.
BasicMelee(
    energy_cost: 90.0,
    buildup_duration: 0.4,
    swing_duration: 0.1,
    hit_timing: 0.5,
    recover_duration: 0.4,
    melee_constructor: (
        kind: Stab(damage: 1, poise: 0, knockback: 0, energy_regen: 0),
        range: 3.0,
        angle: 20.0,
        attack_effect: Some((
            Heal(150.0),
            AttackSource(Melee),
        )),
        attack_effect_target: Some(InGroup),
    ),
    meta: (school: Some(Necromancy), source: Some(Divine)),
)
